{"type":"output_text","text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"wren\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The related-capability searches found gathering, eating and cultivation, but no equivalent food-preparation operation. Eating consumes food without preparing it; cultivation has a different function. Develop a general hand-breaking food operation, with trial and preparation modes, as the smallest equipment-free precursor. It can attempt a genuinely different physical presentation without inventing cooking equipment, fuel, water, improved nutrition or guaranteed success. Whether these roots yield to hand force must be resolved physically, not inferred from their name or edibility.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"Development handoff in this conversation: implement 'Hand-break food', parameterized by mode (trial, prepare, inspect, cancel), owned input stack ID, whole-unit quantity and optional work ID. Trial and preparation share one mechanism and implementation. Reuse and record the existing ownership, reach, food-lot, ageing, work-progress and event routines where applicable; reuse forest.eat for subsequent consumption, extending its food-lot handling only as necessary rather than claiming a new eating mechanism. Dependencies: an explicit deterministic hand-workability rule using material resistance, represented geometry and available hand force; processed-food lot support preserving nutrition, toxicity, origin and age; and persistent work/event records. If these mechanisms are missing, implement them in this handoff. Do not silently assign every edible material a successful result. For existing roots, author a conservative material response from the actual implementation facts; if those facts do not support hand-breaking, the executable outcome is an informative failed trial, not invented pieces or a cooking unlock. No implementation or review waiting advances time. Prerequisites: individ